ORGANIZER;CN="Molina, Javier (NCMI, Clayton)":mailto:Javier.Molina@csiro.au
DESCRIPTION:Living Atlases Information Session - The New ALA Species Lists 
 Application\n\nWhat to expect\nThe ALA’s lists application is a tool tha
 t allows the creation and maintenance of a list of species. This can then 
 be used\, within and external to the ALA.  Key uses of lists include:\n\n 
  1.  Query records for a defined set of species\n  2.  Assign conservation
 / threatened species status to records and species pages\n  3.\nIdentify a
 nd generalising records of sensitive (restricted access) species via the s
 ensitive data service\n  4.  Flag new records of species of biosecurity co
 ncern\n  5.\nProvide a subset of taxa for use in other applications e.g. B
 ioCollect\, Profiles\n\nThe species list application was originally develo
 ped over 15 years ago. It had morphed into a mature application\, largely 
 due to the requirements of other applications (including SDS\, Profiles\, 
 Spatial portal and BioCollect) that needed managed subsets of species link
 ed to the ALA taxonomic backbone to deliver specialised functionality.\n\n
 A review of the Lists product in August 2021 resulted in a decision to upd
 ate and enhance it to better serve current and future requirements. The or
 iginal code had outlived its usefulness and accumulated too much technical
  debt.\n\nThis presentation will walk through: the new application\, the n
 ew user interface\, the new APIs and some uses cases showing how internal 
 and external users can use its functionality.\n\nTime and date\n\nTuesday 
 11 Aug 2026 6-7pm AEST (8-9am  UTC)\n\nSee it in your local time zone<http
 s://www.timeanddate.com/worldclock/fixedtime.html?msg=Living+Atlases+Infor
 mation+Session+-+The+New+ALA+Species+Lists+Application+&iso=20260811T18&p1
 =152&ah=1>.\n\nFurther information\nThis event will be recorded and the re
 cording made available through the Living Atlases slack channel<https://li
 ving-atlases.gbif.org/contact> in the week after the event.\nIf you have a
 ny questions\, please reach out to support@ala.org.au<mailto:support@ala.o
 rg.au>\n\n\n\n____________________________________________________________
